The source changes build, but the campaign metadata can count the active stmap9 iteration before the required canonical version log exists, which violates the project’s iteration contract and can mislead automation/reporting.

Review comment:

- [P2] Keep stmap9 uncounted until it is logged — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/.autoeda/runtime/campaign_state.json:9-11
  With `active_version` set to `stmap9`, the state still reports `completed_iterations`/`next_iteration` as 9 while `.autoeda/runtime/versions.md` has no `version9 / stmap9` entry. Any supervisor/report logic using these fields can treat stmap9 as already counted without the required hypothesis, results, and next-step log; either keep the completed count at the last logged version or add the stmap9 version entry and update the completed/last-completed fields together.
